8.7 Instead of the template functor class that was used in Section 8.3.2 consider using
Functor {
Linss pS ;
:
Functor ( Linss ps ){ pS = ps ;}
() ( lam ) {
( pS - > gcv )( lam );
}
};
which encapsulates the gcv method directly using a Linss object. Combine this functor
class with the Optim class to obtain an alternative version of the Linss smooth method for
minimization of the GCV criterion.
